<p>Hi Lori!<br />
<br />
It was great talking to you and I&#39;m excited to bring a blood drive to your daughter&#39;s school.<br />
<br />
So the first step is to decide if we can do the Future Blood Donor&#39;s program. &nbsp;We don&#39;t have to, but it&#39;s a great program that will certainly help bring in larger numbers. &nbsp;</p>

<p>I&#39;ve attached a short flier and here is a link to a video that is shorter than 2 minutes.</p>

<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1fTXsmcUi7U&amp;feature=youtu.be (you might need to copy and paste)<br />
<br />
Two additional thoughts on it -<br />
1. &nbsp;The presentations are actually only 10 minutes. &nbsp;I think I said 15 on the phone.<br />
2. &nbsp;Every student who recruits an adult to donate will also get a thank you gift. &nbsp;The flier says blanket, but I think it might be a hat. &nbsp;Regardless I&#39;ll double check if we decide to move forward with this.</p>

<p>Once we&#39;ve decided on the doing the full program or not we&#39;ll need to move on to the next steps which will include -<br />
1. &nbsp;Meeting with principal or designee to verify all the OKs.<br />
2. &nbsp;Review the room we&#39;re we&#39;ll host the drive<br />
3. &nbsp;Select a date<br />
4. &nbsp;Review Promotion Plan!<br />
<br />
Thank you for your time and I look forward to hearing back from you.<br />
